{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["macOS"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"arpeggiate"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}]}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"roleHeading":"Case","symbolKind":"case","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"case"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"arpeggiate"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)","externalID":"s:7IvorMXL12MXLNotationsV4ItemO10arpeggiateyAeA13MXLArpeggiateVcAEmF","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}],"role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item"]]},"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)"]}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"arpeggiate"},{"type":"text","text":" alternative."}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"One of the alternatives for Notations.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Item","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLArpeggiate":{"title":"MXLArpeggiate","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}],"type":"topic","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlarpeggiate","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLArpeggiate","abstract":[{"text":"The arpeggiate type indicates that this note is part of an arpeggiated chord. The number attribute can be used","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to distinguish between two simultaneous chords arpeggiated separately (different numbers) or together (same","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"number). The direction attribute is used if there is an arrow on the arpeggio sign. By default, arpeggios go","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the lowest to highest note. The length of the sign can be determined from the position attributes for the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"arpeggiate elements used with the top and bottom notes of the arpeggiated chord. If the unbroken attribute is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"set to yes, it indicates that the arpeggio continues onto another staff within the part. This serves as a hint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to applications and is not required for cross-staff arpeggios.","type":"text"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLArpeggiate"}]},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations":{"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"MXLNotations","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Notations refer to musical notations, not XML notations. Multiple notations are allowed in order to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"multiple editorial levels. The print-object attribute, added in Version 3.0, allows notations to represent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"details of performance technique, such as fingerings, without having them appear in the score.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLNotations","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MXLNotations","kind":"identifier"}],"role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"title":"IvorMXL","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl","type":"topic","role":"collection"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLNotations/Item/arpeggiate(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlnotations\/item\/arpeggiate(_:)","abstract":[{"text":"The ","type":"text"},{"code":"arpeggiate","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" alternative.","type":"text"}],"title":"MXLNotations.Item.arpeggiate(_:)","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLNotations\/Item\/arpeggiate(_:)","type":"topic","fragments":[{"text":"case","kind":"keyword"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"text":"arpeggiate","kind":"identifier"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"text":"MXLArpeggiate","preciseIdentifier":"s:7IvorMXL13MXLArpeggiateV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"kind":"text","text":")"}],"role":"symbol"}}}